From c737360e571400cfb5d642eee1ccd9558c2dd2b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:12:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] pco: propagate register reads into their uses

A read of a virtual register was an opaque mbyp, so a value held in a
register (a loop-carried value or the result of an if) was always copied
to a temporary before use. The read is now a mov, and forward
propagation substitutes the register for the temporary when the use is
in the same block and nothing writes the register in between. The
compare into p0 before an if accepts a register source on the same
condition, up to the end of the compare's block when the if follows it.

The dual issue scheduler sank an instruction below a later one checking
only that nothing between read its result; an instruction that now reads
a register directly must also not move past a write to that register.

glmark2 loop fragment-uniform=true (zink, off-screen): the loop body goes
from 9 to 6 instruction groups per iteration, 502 -> 650 FPS; bump
normals +3%. Other scenes unchanged. CTS unchanged (same lists as the
uniform loop commit).
